<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-jiuquan ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D / unknown payload (Jiuquan LA-94, SLS-2 / 603) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Event times: SAST TYPICAL LM-2D sequence via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/长征二号丁: pitch-over 17.0 s, S1 cutoff 153.9 s, sep 155.1 s, fairing 185.1 s, S2 main cutoff 324.1 s, S2 vernier cutoff 705.1 s (payload sep 737.1 s not in this file).
Azimuth 192.23 deg: great-circle bearing from pad to centroid 35.554N 98.863E (614 km) of NOTAM ZLHW A5728/26 danger area (valid 2026-11-11 11:32-12:05Z = LL2 window; https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZLHW-A5728%2F26), INFERRED stage-1 impact zone; implies i~99 deg (SSO class).
Orbit unpublished (LL2 &#x27;Unknown&#x27;): vernier-cutoff altitude 500 km circular ASSUMED (= LM-2D published 1.9 t / 500 km SSO reference, huijiwiki). Payload unknown (LL2 &#x27;Unknown Payload&#x27;).
T0: LL2 NET 2026-11-11T11:40:00Z (window 11:32-12:05Z = Wed 11 Nov 3:40 am PST).
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times, final = assumed orbit): 0:0, 17:0.3, 153.9:55.2, 155.1:56.2, 185.1:80.6, 324.1:213.8, 705.1:500
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.687 km/s (circular v at 500 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+705.1 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 40.960482N 100.298059E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=192.23 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-11T11:40:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
